<title>UK: Texaco, Gulf apologise for UK refinery blast.</title>
<headline>Texaco, Gulf apologise for UK refinery blast.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Texaco Ltd and Chevron Corp unit Gulf Oil (Great Britain) Ltd, each fined 100,000 stg after a huge explosion at their Pembroke oil refinery in July 1994, apologised for the accident on Friday.</p>
<p>In a joint statement the companies said they deeply regretted that the accident occurred.</p>
<p>&quot;We have always been proud of our high standard s of operation at the the Pembroke plant. since the incident we have continued to work closely with the Health and Safety Executive to share lessons that can be learned and to minimise the possibility of such as incident happening again&quot;.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4984</p>
